  "public_messages": [
    "I’ll inspect the supplied task and tooling instructions, collect the frozen source-room evidence, then build the analysis pipeline and deliverables in the workspace. I’ll preserve the provided instructions, keep synthetic and public evidence distinct, and verify calculations plus rendered outputs before handing everything over.",
    "The source room is a small frozen set of client exports, correction/assumption files, ECB history, and archived World Bank responses. I’m downloading the complete index contents first so the analysis can be provenance-first and reproducible.",
    "The extracts contain the intended traps: repeated rows across pages, 18 higher-revision order corrections, cancelled/test/future rows, duplicate and revised returns, one orphan return, one late return beyond cutoff, and valid zero-price shipments. I’ll encode the dictionary’s “highest revision wins / identical repeats collapse” rules explicitly and preserve an audit log of each exclusion.",
    "The first reproducible run is complete. It selects CZE+ESP on the stated “highest feasible base-case annual contribution” rule: EUR225k capex, 5 FTE, EUR198.1k base annual incremental contribution, 1.14-year simple payback; low/stress remain positive but much weaker. I’m now turning the same outputs into the board report, deck, and workbook, with the strongest alternatives and decision gates visible.",
    "The report PDF, PPTX, XLSX, metrics JSON, normalized CSV outputs, and provenance register are now generated from the same analysis run. I’m doing a verification pass next: schema/metric reconciliation, workbook formula/chart readability, PDF page extraction/rendering, and presentation structure.",
    "Completed the Meridian Parts evidence pack.\n\nRecommendation: staged CZE + ESP hubs — €225k capex, 5 FTE, €198.1k base annual incremental contribution, 1.14-year simple payback. Low case: €64.6k; defined stress: €32.2k.\n\nDeliverables:\n\n- [Executive report PDF](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_parts_board_report.pdf)\n- [Board presentation PPTX](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_parts_board_presentation.pptx)\n- [Analytical workbook XLSX](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_parts_analysis.xlsx)\n- [metrics.json](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/metrics.json)\n- [Reproduction instructions](<CELL>/workspace/REPRODUCE.md)\n- [Source register with hashes](<CELL>/workspace/evidence/source-register-collected.json)\n\nVerification passed: monthly/country reconciliation, metrics schema counts, scenario coverage, workbook chart presence, 7-page PDF text extraction, and 8-slide PPTX structure. Known anomalies and limitations are documented, including the orphan return, late return, synthetic demand inputs, and lack of DCF/casual inference."
  ],
